---
// The results explorer.
//
// The shell is rendered here and the table is drawn in the browser, because every slice the
// controls offer is a different table over the same run and building them all at once would
// ship forty copies of one number.
import Shell from "../components/Shell.astro";
import { BLENDS, labelOf } from "../lib/blends.ts";
import { provenance } from "../lib/catalog.ts";
import { jsonScript } from "../lib/html.ts";
import { site } from "../lib/site.ts";

const { pageData, config } = site();
// What this build knows. A build pointed at another results site knows nothing yet, and the
// explorer rewrites both of these once that site's catalog arrives.
const { eyebrow, runs } = provenance(pageData.boot.catalog);
const built = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace("T", " ") + " UTC";
---

<Shell
  title="RequestBench Results"
  description="Sortable, filterable HTTP framework results across languages, hosts and time."
  dataBase={config.dataBase}
  footerLeft="github.com/ipjohnson/RequestBench"
  footerRight={`<span id="nruns">${runs}</span> runs &middot; raw histograms in the run files`}
>
  <p class="eyebrow"><span id="provenance">{eyebrow}</span> &middot; built {built}</p>
  <h1>RequestBench Results</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every framework in a run shares one machine and one window, so these are real latencies and
    they rank directly against each other. Nothing here is divided by anything: what a framework
    took is what is shown. The <a href="tests.html">tests</a> page shows what each request sends and
    what its answer has to pass.
  </p>

  <div class="controls">
    <div class="ctl">
      <label for="host">Execution host</label>
      <select id="host"></select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctl">
      <label for="rung">Offered rate</label>
      <select id="rung"></select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctl">
      <label for="metric">Metric</label>
      <select id="metric">
        <option value="p50Us">p50</option>
        <option value="p90Us">p90</option>
        <option value="p99Us">p99</option>
        <option value="p999Us">p99.9</option>
        <option value="achievedRps">achieved rps</option>
        <option value="dropped">dropped</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctl">
      <label>Granularity</label>
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Granularity">
        <button data-gran="blend">Blend</button>
        <button data-gran="family">Family</button>
        <button data-gran="test">Test</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctl"><label>Languages</label><div class="chips" id="chips"></div></div>
    <div class="ctl">
      <label for="q" id="qlabel">Filter</label>
      <input type="search" id="q" list="qopts" autocomplete="off" placeholder="test or framework" />
      <datalist id="qopts"></datalist>
    </div>
    <div class="ctl"><label>Columns</label><div class="chips" id="colchips"></div></div>
    <div class="spacer"></div>
    <div class="ctl">
      <label>&nbsp;</label>
      <div class="seg"><button id="reset" type="button">Reset</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctl picker" id="picker" hidden>
      <label>Custom blend</label>
      <div class="from">
        Start from
        {BLENDS.filter((b) => b !== "custom").map((b) => <button type="button" class="chip sm" data-from={b}>{labelOf(b)}</button>)}
        <button type="button" class="chip sm" data-from="none">None</button>
        <span>Each test counts once, times its family's weight.</span>
      </div>
      <div id="pickfams"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="scroll">
    <table>
      <thead id="thead"></thead>
      <tbody id="tbody"></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="count" id="meta" style="margin-top:10px">Loading the results catalog&hellip;</p>
  <div class="note" id="hostnote" hidden></div>
  <div class="note" id="runnote" hidden></div>

  <div class="panel">
    <div class="panelhead">
      <h2>Over time</h2>
      <div class="ctl">
        <label for="machine">Machine</label>
        <select id="machine"></select>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">
      The top six rows of the current ranking, over the runs on one machine with the newest run's
      rate ladder and corpus. The same framework on another CPU can take twice as long, so two
      machines never share a chart.
    </p>
    <div id="time"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    Each row is the time that framework took at the offered rate, on the machine and in the window
    named above. A framework that could not sustain a rate has no latency at it: percentiles over
    the requests that survived would flatter the collapse, so what it achieved and what it
    dropped is shown instead.
  </div>

  <script id="rb-data" type="application/json" set:html={jsonScript(pageData)} />
  <script>
    import { start } from "../client/explorer.ts";

    const raw = document.getElementById("rb-data")?.textContent ?? "{}";
    void start(JSON.parse(raw));
  </script>
</Shell>
